  "headline": "CORRECTED after inspecting actual numbers (superseding the pre-run speculative text that was in the script comment). detilt(+/-L) is EXACTLY 0.0 (float64-exact) for every family and every N -- expected, since the de-tilt step algebraically subtracts the linear interpolant between the raw endpoints, forcing new endpoints to 0 by construction regardless of anything else. The real question is the RAW (pre-detilt) endpoint values / mismatch, i.e. whether K(+/-L;t)=0 already holds in the un-corrected kernel. Result: for SMOOTH profiles with no derivative discontinuity (logistic at k=1,4,10,30; the alpha=1.5 opposite-bumps gain-carrying case) the raw mismatch is at the float64 noise floor (~1e-15) already at N=2001, with NO growth or trend across N up to 64001 -- consistent with the raw kernel being exactly zero at the seam for these profiles. For profiles with a genuine derivative discontinuity at some interior point (plateau_a0.5L: sharp edge at x=+/-a*L; offcentre_step: a steep tanh edge, w=0.02) the raw mismatch is NONZERO but DECAYS CLEANLY AS O(1/N) -- e.g. plateau_a0.5L: 8.90e-4 (N=2001) -> 4.45e-4 (4001) -> 2.23e-4 (8001) -> 1.11e-4 (16001) -> 5.56e-5 (32001) -> 2.78e-5 (64001), a clean halving each time N doubles (Gibbs/quadrature error from the Hilbert-transform FFT and cumulative-trapezoid steps near a discontinuity), extrapolating to exactly 0 as N -> infinity. CONCLUSION: V5 is SUPPORTED. eps''(+/-L)=0 holds automatically in the continuum limit -- the raw (un-detilted) kernel already gives K(+/-L;t)=0, matching the Wave-3 claim. The de-tilt step genuinely IS \"a no-op that only absorbs discretization error\": for smooth profiles it has nothing to absorb (already at machine zero); for profiles with sharp features it absorbs an O(1/N) quadrature artifact that vanishes with resolution, not an O(1) physical effect. No family tested (smooth, plateau, off-centre step, or gain-carrying/non-passive) broke this. CAVEAT / scope: only checked eps''(+/-L) itself (V5), not whether the de-tilt could still matter for OTHER quantities (e.g. it clearly does shift the interior profile by a nonzero linear ramp whenever raw_endpoint_mismatch != 0, which changes min(eps'') at finite N by a commensurate O(1/N) amount -- this is a genuine, if vanishing, effect on the H6 crossover calculation and should be kept in mind for near-threshold alpha_c values at low N)."
